", "type": "VIEW", "color": "blue", "position": 0, "universalIdentifier": "410b6a7f-54b9-427e-a2f6-f81d7abd8a7a", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "5d1609d3-e1fa-4743-92d9-cfbac57ee4e4", "folderUniversalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}, {"icon": "IconFolder", "name": "Projects", "type": "VIEW", "color": "green", "position": 1, "universalIdentifier": "4f722a60-0eda-4e87-bb1a-94d19391d2d3", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "bf0f39da-1310-4246-9b56-21f9b6fd689e", "folderUniversalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}, {"icon": "IconLayoutDashboard", "name": "Work Board", "type": "PAGE_LAYOUT", "color": "blue", "position": -10, "universalIdentifier": "6aa89f2a-3043-4498-addb-6899a10ab638", "pageLayoutUniversalIdentifier": "11a4b44a-78d5-4e36-84a0-cb88d85a4111"}, {"icon": "IconClock", "name": "Time Entries", "type": "VIEW", "color": "turquoise", "position": 5, "universalIdentifier": "97268a3d-4eb3-417f-a0f7-73e0a0a0f5c8", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "38fdac5b-0a9b-4ba1-9121-78e71c24b9c3", "folderUniversalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}, {"icon": "IconUsers", "name": "Contractor Management", "type": "FOLDER", "color": "blue", "position": 10, "universalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}, {"icon": "IconBriefcase", "name": "Assignments", "type": "VIEW", "color": "orange", "position": 2, "universalIdentifier": "f4a9af93-af5a-4225-a7ef-53bbc57b688e", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "221373b1-eaf8-4695-b52a-4f48f35b94fc", "folderUniversalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}, {"icon": "IconMessageCircle", "name": "Timestopper Changelog", "type": "VIEW", "color": "green", "position": 10, "universalIdentifier": "f516d471-785d-485d-829b-508db9025d60", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "2c80daf9-2060-4db7-8b54-3da8a238407a"}, {"icon": "IconFileExport", "name": "Export Templates", "type": "VIEW", "color": "gray", "position": 6, "universalIdentifier": "f95b6284-3875-4c40-bfe1-47a542054562", "viewUniversalIdentifier": "9834bfd6-b4fc-4eea-ba82-e51c4d53e5cb", "folderUniversalIdentifier": "c297bea5-6638-4912-af14-e4e38b06191b"}], "timelineActivityTypes": []}	f	f	public/logo.svg	Contractor management — onboarding, projects, assignments, rates, time tracking & approvals	Emerant	Productivity	https://emerant.net	# Timestopper — Contractor & Timesheet Management\n\nTimestopper runs contractor management inside [Twenty CRM](https://twenty.com). It covers onboarding, projects, assignments and rates, plus weekly timesheets, approvals, payment tracking and exports you design yourself.\n\nBuilt by **[Emerant](https://emerant.net)**. Requires Twenty **2.45 or later**.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Work Board**: contractors see only their own weekly timesheet, entries and hour totals, and submit hours for approval. The **Submit Hours** command logs hours from anywhere in Twenty.\n- **Management**: admins can do the following:\n  - filter every time entry by project, contractor, period, status and payment state;\n  - review revenue rankings;\n  - bulk-approve, mark entries paid or invoiced, or delete them.\n- **Approvals and payments**: approval and payment dates and the approver's name are recorded automatically.\n- **Export Templates**: the Export menu lists templates you manage as records in Twenty. CSV and Excel exports are built in. For any other layout, a named template sends the filtered entries as JSON to your n8n workflow.\n- **Roles**:\n  - *Contractor Admin*: full access.\n  - *Contractor*: Work Board only; management data stays hidden.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. In Twenty, open **Settings → Applications → Marketplace**, find **Timestopper** and click **Install**.\n2. Assign roles in **Settings → Members**:\n   - **Contractor Admin** for people who manage contractors, approvals and exports;\n   - **Contractor** for contractors.\n3. For each contractor, create a **Contractor** record (**Contractor Management → Contractors**) and set its **Workspace Member**. A contractor whose e-mail matches a member's login e-mail is linked automatically.\n4. Create **Projects** (optionally linked to a Company) and **Assignments** that link a contractor to a project with dates and rates. Contractors can log hours on their active assignments.\n\nNo API keys are needed. The app uses Twenty's built-in application access, and every contractor only ever sees their own data.\n\nTo receive new versions automatically, open the app's **General** tab and turn on **auto-upgrade**.\n\n## Everyday use\n\n| Who | Where | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Contractor | **Work Board → Work Panel** | Fill in the weekly timesheet, then submit hours up to a date. Submitted days are locked. |\n| Contractor | **Submit Hours** command | Quick-add hours for one assignment. |\n| Admin | **Approval Manager** command / **Work Board → Management** | Approve or reject entries, mark them invoiced or paid, export. |\n| Admin | **Contractor Management** sidebar | Contractors, Projects, Assignments, Time Entries, Export Templates. |\n\n## Export templates\n\nOpen **Contractor Management → Export Templates**. Every active template appears in the Management dashboard's **Export** menu, and exports always use the filters you have set on the dashboard. **Settings → Applications → Timestopper → Export Templates** lists the configured templates and the field reference.\n\nTwo templates are created on first install. Edit or delete them like any other record:\n\n| Template | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Hours (CSV) | Filtered entries as a CSV file |\n| Hours (Excel) | Filtered entries as an Excel (`.xlsx`) file with rates and totals |\n\n### Download templates (CSV / Excel)\n\nThe app builds the file and gives you a download link. The file is also kept on the template's **Last Export** field.\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** | Label in the Export menu |\n| **Format** | `CSV` or `Excel (.xlsx)` |\n| **Columns** | Comma-separated, left to right: `field` or `field:Header`. Use `-` to leave a column empty. Fields: `date, contractorName, projectName, clientName, assignmentRole, description, hours, hoursHHMM, startTime, finishTime, status, paidStatus, costRate, billRate, totalCost, totalBill, currency, approvedAt, approvedByName, paidAt, invoiceReference`. `startTime(08:30)` / `finishTime(08:30)` set the day start used to derive times from hours. |\n\n### n8n webhook templates\n\nUse these for any other layout or destination, such as a client's timesheet, an invoice or a PDF. Set **Delivery** to `Webhook` and give the template a **unique name**. When someone runs it, the app sends the export to your n8n webhook (or any HTTP endpoint) as a JSON `POST`:\n\n```json\n{\n  "export": "Monthly invoice",\n  "templateId": "…",\n  "requestedBy": "Jane Admin",\n  "requestedAt": "2026-10-07T10:00:00.000Z",\n  "filters": { "fromDate": "2026-09-01", "toDate": "2026-09-30", "status": null, "paidStatus": null, "projectIds": [], "contractorIds": ["…"] },\n  "summary": { "entryCount": 42, "totalHours": 160, "totalCost": 6400, "totalBill": 10480, "currencies": ["EUR"] },\n  "entries": [\n    { "date": "2026-09-01", "contractorName": "…", "projectName": "…", "clientName": "…", "assignmentRole": "…", "description": "…",\n      "hours": 8, "status": "APPROVED", "paidStatus": "UNPAID", "costRate": 40, "billRate": 65.5, "currency": "EUR",\n      "totalCost": 320, "totalBill": 524, "approvedAt": "…", "approvedByName": "…", "paidAt": null, "invoiceReference": "", "id": "…" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nBranch your flow on `export` (the template name). The flow's answer decides what the user sees:\n\n- **A file** (for example from n8n's *Respond to Webhook* node with binary data): offered as a download and kept on **Last Export**.\n- **JSON with `url`**: offered as a download link.\n- **Anything else**: the user sees a confirmation, or your JSON `message` if there is one.\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Webhook URL** | Where the export is sent. Falls back to the app's **Default export webhook URL** setting. |\n\nConfiguration mistakes, such as an unknown column, a missing webhook URL or a duplicate name, are shown in the dashboard with a readable message.\n\n## Settings\n\n| Setting | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Default export webhook URL** (optional) | Used by n8n webhook templates that have no webhook URL of their own. Set it in **Settings → Applications → Timestopper**. |\n\n## Support\n\nTimestopper is developed by **Emerant**. For questions, support or custom features, visit **[emerant.net](https://emerant.net)**.\n	\N	\N	\N	{}	[{"path": "public/cover.generated.png", "fileId": "36b984a6-b53d-4504-b5a5-c7521f6908d9"}]	3b1f5cb5-7e1c-4af1-aa8a-cee22c4e6352	\N
