7213"}, {"icon": "IconMessage", "name": "lastContactItemMessage", "type": "MORPH_RELATION", "label": "Last contact item", "morphId": "085b9e30-8371-4c0f-84f1-392e01bd70d2", "isNullable": true, "description": "The email or meeting that was the most recent contact with a person from this company.", "isUIEditable": false, "universalSettings": {"onDelete": "SET_NULL", "relationType": "MANY_TO_ONE", "joinColumnName": "lastContactItemMessageId"}, "universalIdentifier": "e57d1842-1f16-4763-b0f5-89d2cf9abd07", "objectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-b374-4779-a561-80086cb2e17f", "relationTargetFieldMetadataUniversalIdentifier": "6b1779f6-da9b-41e2-a620-3d27eadda03a", "relationTargetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-3f6b-4425-80ab-e468899ab4b2"}, {"icon": "IconClockPlay", "name": "firstContactAt", "type": "DATE_TIME", "label": "First contact", "isNullable": true, "description": "When the earliest contact (email or meeting) with this person occurred, in either direction.", "isUIEditable": false, "universalIdentifier": "f8333cb6-7ff0-408e-b75f-7f390b241c43", "objectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-e674-48e5-a542-72570eee7213"}, {"icon": "IconActivity", "name": "interactionCount", "type": "NUMBER", "label": "Interaction count", "isNullable": true, "description": "Total synced interactions with people from this record.", "defaultValue": 0, "isUIEditable": false, "universalIdentifier": "fa3b68ad-3b79-448f-8de0-4108d08d0568", "objectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-9549-49dd-b2b2-883999db8938"}, {"icon": "IconActivity", "name": "interactionCount", "type": "NUMBER", "label": "Interaction count", "isNullable": true, "description": "Total synced interactions with people from this record.", "defaultValue": 0, "isUIEditable": false, "universalIdentifier": "faa0de40-c938-4452-b468-e4a150df77ee", "objectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-b374-4779-a561-80086cb2e17f"}, {"icon": "IconCalendar", "name": "meetingCount", "type": "NUMBER", "label": "Meeting count", "isNullable": true, "description": "Number of synced meetings with this person.", "defaultValue": 0, "isUIEditable": false, "universalIdentifier": "ff3c6734-0d1f-4545-a611-473a2643e88a", "objectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-e674-48e5-a542-72570eee7213"}], "skills": [], "indexes": [], "objects": [], "viewFields": [], "application": {"logo": "public/logo.png", "author": "Excelium Tech", "category": "Productivity", "description": "Full relationship intelligence on People, Companies and Opportunities. Adds first and last contact, next meeting, email and meeting counts, connection strength and strongest connection, plus who reached out and the exact email or meeting behind it, kept up to date automatically from your synced emails and meetings.", "displayName": "Communication Intelligence", "galleryImages": ["public/gallery/cover.png"], "aboutDescription": "# Communication Intelligence\\n\\n**Full relationship intelligence on your People, Companies and Opportunities — live from your synced email and calendar.**\\n\\n## ✨ What you get\\n\\n- **First and last contact** — when the relationship started and the most recent touch, in either direction\\n- **Direction and attribution** — who reached out (you or them), the last contact by teammate, and the strongest connection on your team\\n- **Volume and cadence** — email count, meeting count, total interactions, and the next scheduled meeting\\n- **Connection strength** — a recency- and frequency-weighted score (No connection → Very strong)\\n- **Zero upkeep** — updates in real time from every synced email and meeting, with your full history backfilled the moment you install\\n\\n## 📊 The columns (on People)\\n\\n- **First contact** / **Last contact** — earliest and most recent touch, either direction\\n- **First email** / **First meeting** / **Next meeting** — timeline anchors from your synced data\\n- **Last outbound** / **Last inbound** — when you last reached out vs. when they last did\\n- **Email count** / **Meeting count** / **Interaction count** — volume of synced touches\\n- **Connection strength** — No connection, Very weak, Weak, Good, Strong, or Very strong\\n- **Strongest connection** / **Last contact by** — the teammate with the strongest relationship, and the one behind the most recent touch\\n- **Last contact item** / **Last email** / **Last meeting** — one click to the actual record\\n\\nOn **Companies** and **Opportunities** you also get **Last contact** and **Last contact item**, plus rolled-up **First contact**, **Next meeting**, **Interaction count**, and **Connection strength** (aggregated across the account's people; Opportunities roll up from their point of contact).\\n\\n## 💳 Billing\\n\\n**Free** — no credits, no metering.\\n\\n## 📌 Heads up\\n\\nNeeds a synced inbox or calendar (Google, Outlook, or CalDAV). Direction is inferred from the email's sender and the meeting's organizer; a meeting counts as both. Connection strength weights each interaction by recency (30-day half-life) and frequency; thresholds are tunable in `compute-connection-strength.ts`.\\n", "yarnLockChecksum": "64f97265cb7597c0e0bea4d8871bfeaf", "packageJsonChecksum": "6cd01c877dc8ef254cf7f760c9b3c3eb", "universalIdentifier": "b5097f21-704f-4ec4-9734-6f1d78523571", "postInstallLogicFunction": {"universalIdentifier": "79d615c5-020b-4027-9e75-1d0b9daeadcf", "shouldRunSynchronously": false, "shouldRunOnVersionUpgrade": true}, "requiredServerVersionRange": ">=2.20.0", "defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier": "7b2675f5-a5a0-4167-8b64-544927387545"}, "pageLayouts": [], "publicAssets": [{"checksum": "75971611a06602a33cf7482f65e7a902", "fileName": "cover.png", "filePath": "public/gallery/cover.png", "fileType": "png"}, {"checksum": "bdca61cbe8ae8e5b943420d03172ff76", "fileName": "logo.png", "filePath": "public/logo.png", "fileType": "png"}], "logicFunctions": [{"name": "backfill-communication-intelligence", "description": "Fills person communication-intelligence fields (first/last/next, counts, connection strength, strongest connection) and company and opportunity last-contact fields from existing messages and calendar events after installation.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 300, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/backfill-last-contact.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/backfill-last-contact.ts", "universalIdentifier": "79d615c5-020b-4027-9e75-1d0b9daeadcf", "builtHandlerChecksum": "927c80d3e55db13828f78f85c5eda32d", "shouldRunOnVersionUpgrade": true}, {"name": "on-calendar-event-started", "description": "Updates last-contacted fields and recomputes communication intelligence (moving the next meeting to last, refreshing counts and strength) for participants of calendar events whose start time just passed.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 60, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-calendar-event-started.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-calendar-event-started.ts", "cronTriggerSettings": {"pattern": "*/5 * * * *"}, "universalIdentifier": "7a67601b-f59d-4909-8230-11eb35fa7c21", "builtHandlerChecksum": "d3e8dcfdf48f90e00073c29755eb4d6b"}, {"name": "on-calendar-interaction", "description": "Updates a person's last-contacted fields and recomputes their communication intelligence (first/next, counts, connection strength, strongest connection), plus last contact on their company and opportunities, when a new calendar event participant is matched.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 60, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-calendar-interaction.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-calendar-interaction.ts", "universalIdentifier": "a10f1a0e-9679-4bff-8c0c-e3b42b7b5273", "builtHandlerChecksum": "f10ebf2e11d151dfbad56b1afc059ab1", "databaseEventTriggerSettings": {"eventName": "calendarEventParticipant.updated", "updatedFields": ["personId"]}}, {"name": "recompute-companies", "description": "Recomputes communication intelligence for the selected companies: recomputes each company's people from raw messages and calendar events, then rolls up to the company and related opportunities.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 300, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/recompute-companies.function.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/recompute-companies.function.ts", "universalIdentifier": "e8f3311c-cd8d-43f4-ad20-8716f9351ef0", "builtHandlerChecksum": "afaf39a9403ae9549718c534946d6544", "httpRouteTriggerSettings": {"path": "/communication-intelligence/recompute-companies", "httpMethod": "POST", "isAuthRequired": true}}, {"name": "on-email-interaction", "description": "Updates a person's last-contacted fields and recomputes their communication intelligence (first/next, counts, connection strength, strongest connection), plus last contact on their company and opportunities, when a new email participant is matched.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 60, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-email-interaction.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/on-email-interaction.ts", "universalIdentifier": "f8f14257-e14d-48b5-bf42-52827eb4d0fd", "builtHandlerChecksum": "05cbbdb7584b6d0f0f24c2ada8c2c7fd", "databaseEventTriggerSettings": {"eventName": "messageParticipant.updated", "updatedFields": ["personId"]}}], "pageLayoutTabs": [], "frontComponents": [{"name": "recompute-company-intelligence", "isHeadless": true, "description": "Recomputes communication intelligence for the selected companies.", "componentName": "RecomputeCompanyIntelligence", "usesSdkClient": false, "builtComponentPath": "src/front-components/recompute-company-intelligence.front-component.mjs", "sourceComponentPath": "src/front-components/recompute-company-intelligence.front-component.tsx", "universalIdentifier": "60d6206d-f3d7-4043-b578-84852d93001e", "builtComponentChecksum": "b52f66f8113f3b05a68213a422539bdd1924dd3d648233ab2dad0c4262604603"}], "permissionFlags": [], "commandMenuItems": [{"label": "Recompute communication intelligence", "availabilityType": "RECORD_SELECTION", "universalIdentifier": "441eaf69-2d7e-4002-9a92-64acd6c25291", "frontComponentUniversalIdentifier": "60d6206d-f3d7-4043-b578-84852d93001e", "availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier": "20202020-b374-4779-a561-80086cb2e17f"}], "connectionProviders": [], "navigationMenuItems": []}	f	f	public/logo.png	Full relationship intelligence on People, Companies and Opportunities. Adds first and last contact, next meeting, email and meeting counts, connection strength and strongest connection, plus who reached out and the exact email or meeting behind it, kept up to date automatically from your synced emails and meetings.	Excelium Tech	Productivity	\N	# Communication Intelligence\n\n**Full relationship intelligence on your People, Companies and Opportunities — live from your synced email and calendar.**\n\n## ✨ What you get\n\n- **First and last contact** — when the relationship started and the most recent touch, in either direction\n- **Direction and attribution** — who reached out (you or them), the last contact by teammate, and the strongest connection on your team\n- **Volume and cadence** — email count, meeting count, total interactions, and the next scheduled meeting\n- **Connection strength** — a recency- and frequency-weighted score (No connection → Very strong)\n- **Zero upkeep** — updates in real time from every synced email and meeting, with your full history backfilled the moment you install\n\n## 📊 The columns (on People)\n\n- **First contact** / **Last contact** — earliest and most recent touch, either direction\n- **First email** / **First meeting** / **Next meeting** — timeline anchors from your synced data\n- **Last outbound** / **Last inbound** — when you last reached out vs. when they last did\n- **Email count** / **Meeting count** / **Interaction count** — volume of synced touches\n- **Connection strength** — No connection, Very weak, Weak, Good, Strong, or Very strong\n- **Strongest connection** / **Last contact by** — the teammate with the strongest relationship, and the one behind the most recent touch\n- **Last contact item** / **Last email** / **Last meeting** — one click to the actual record\n\nOn **Companies** and **Opportunities** you also get **Last contact** and **Last contact item**, plus rolled-up **First contact**, **Next meeting**, **Interaction count**, and **Connection strength** (aggregated across the account's people; Opportunities roll up from their point of contact).\n\n## 💳 Billing\n\n**Free** — no credits, no metering.\n\n## 📌 Heads up\n\nNeeds a synced inbox or calendar (Google, Outlook, or CalDAV). Direction is inferred from the email's sender and the meeting's organizer; a meeting counts as both. Connection strength weights each interaction by recency (30-day half-life) and frequency; thresholds are tunable in `compute-connection-strength.ts`.\n	\N	\N	\N	{}	[{"path": "public/gallery/cover.png", "fileId": "b0d45ada-ade3-4628-83a4-d551bd9e4048"}]	482414fb-fd1f-4f55-8c85-47fee81e3083	\N
763aae4a-8f7e-49eb-909d-7d1a8081729f	51583e7b-80b4-4df9-a166-7e1af5bcc70e	Nodpack for Twenty	49e43365-377f-4af9-adb4-32aa1e44555b	\N	{}	{}	\N	2026-10-31 12:36:10.161208+00	2026-10-31 13:26:44.947294+00	\N	\N	npm	nodpack-for-twenty	\N	0.1.2	f	{"roles": [{"label": "Nodpack for Twenty default function role", "description": "Nodpack for Twenty default function role", "fieldPermissions": [], "objectPermissions": [], "universalIdentifier": "17f69cc0-8816-4916-a9c1-100cd7e5a67a", "canReadAllObjectRecords": true, "canUpdateAllObjectRecords": true, "canDestroyAllObjectRecords": false, "rowLevelPermissionPredicates": [], "canSoftDeleteAllObjectRecords": true, "rowLevelPermissionPredicateGroups": [], "permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers": []}], "views": [], "agents": [], "fields": [], "skills": [], "indexes": [], "objects": [], "viewFields": [], "application": {"logo": "public/logo.png", "description": "Sets up the objects, fields, views and role the Nodpack mobile app needs in your Twenty workspace.", "displayName": "Nodpack for Twenty", "galleryImages": ["public/cover.generated.png"], "aboutDescription": "# Nodpack for Twenty\\n\\nA companion [Twenty](https://twenty.com) app for [Nodpack](https://nodpack.com), the mobile CRM app for Twenty. It is planned as a **schema-only pack**: it would set up the objects, fields, views and role that Nodpack needs in a Twenty workspace (message templates, logged calls and texts), so every workspace gets the same defaults, with no logic functions so that it can install on a stock self-hosted Twenty as well as on Twenty Cloud. Whether it becomes the setup path is decided in TWE-100.\\n\\nNodpack is an independent product of Protomated. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Twenty.\\n\\nStatus (Oct 2026): scaffolded, not yet modelled. The spike that decides whether this pack is the setup path for Nodpack (TWE-99, TWE-100) is in progress. Work is tracked in Nifty, project **TWE**.\\n\\n## What is here\\n\\n| Path | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| `src/` | The app: application config, default role, constants; objects, fields, views and navigation items go here as they are added. |\\n| `src/__tests__/` | Unit tests and integration tests (the latter need a Twenty server). |\\n| `public/`, `locales/` | App logo (`logo.png`, Protomated's mark) and translations. |\\n| `docs/design/research/` | Numbered notes: what the app is for, what it may contain, and what the spike must prove. |\\n| `docs/dev/` | Developer guides: [publishing and claiming](docs/dev/publishing.md). |\\n| `docs/gtm/` | [Naming rules](docs/gtm/01-naming-rules.md) for the app's public name. |\\n| `.github/workflows/` | CI, a deploy-and-install check, and npm publishing with provenance. |\\n\\nDocumentation index: [docs/README.md](docs/README.md). Coding agents: see [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).\\n\\n## Getting started\\n\\nSetup steps are in [SETUP.md](SETUP.md). In short:\\n\\n```sh\\nyarn install\\nyarn twenty docker:start   # local Twenty at http://localhost:2020\\nyarn twenty dev            # sync the app and watch for changes\\n```\\n\\nCheck your work with `yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck`, `yarn test:unit` and (with the server running) `yarn test`.\\n\\n## Publishing\\n\\nThe `Publish` workflow publishes to npm with provenance using [npm trusted publishing](https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers). Publishing from this public repo is also what lets a Twenty admin claim the app. Steps, owners and gotchas: [docs/dev/publishing.md](docs/dev/publishing.md).\\n\\n## Working on it\\n\\n- Branches: `twe-<n>/<short-name>` for the Nifty task, merged into `main` with a merge commit.\\n- Commit messages: `TWE-<n>: <what changed, in plain words>`, with a body that says why.\\n- This repo is public. Do not commit secrets, real customer data or internal planning material.\\n\\n## Changelog\\n\\nNotable changes are documented in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).\\n\\n## Licence\\n\\nApache-2.0. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).\\n\\n## Learn more\\n\\n- [Twenty Apps documentation](https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/apps/getting-started/quick-start)\\n- [twenty-sdk CLI reference](https://www.npmjs.com/package/twenty-sdk)\\n- [Twenty Discord](https://discord.gg/cx5n4Jzs57)\\n", "yarnLockChecksum": "67848385adbd96d8639b166fc59c38f6", "packageJsonChecksum": "64ba329fe0e1d4d54604459532956460", "universalIdentifier": "51583e7b-80b4-4df9-a166-7e1af5bcc70e", "healthCheckLogicFunction": {"universalIdentifier": "729c8970-309d-4694-bc20-81154a8c5329"}, "requiredServerVersionRange": null, "defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier": "17f69cc0-8816-4916-a9c1-100cd7e5a67a"}, "pageLayouts": [{"name": "Nodpack for Twenty", "tabs": [{"icon": "IconApps", "title": "Overview", "widgets": [{"type": "FRONT_COMPONENT", "title": " ", "position": {"index": 0, "layoutMode": "VERTICAL_LIST", "heightBehavior": "TAB_VIEWPORT"}, "configuration": {"configurationType": "FRONT_COMPONENT", "frontComponentUniversalIdentifier": "e9178c9b-b6ea-4cf9-a1df-5411e3717983"}, "universalIdentifier": "d292db24-3977-43d5-86f6-9486c2326c24"}], "position": 0, "layoutMode": "VERTICAL_LIST", "universalIdentifier": "c0aa2106-9b53-437f-b6d9-157cb6e5830d"}], "type": "STANDALONE_PAGE", "universalIdentifier": "984c2456-1b2f-4f2b-9870-da5ce117cb07"}], "publicAssets": [{"checksum": "b40289e43b84b500616b3b2b56271cba", "fileName": "logo.png", "filePath": "public/logo.png", "fileType": "png"}, {"checksum": "c709f56df21bbfa662a673c52b4baec5", "fileName": "cover.generated.png", "filePath": "public/cover.generated.png", "fileType": "png"}], "translations": {}, "logicFunctions": [{"name": "health-check", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/health-check.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/health-check.ts", "universalIdentifier": "729c8970-309d-4694-bc20-81154a8c5329", "builtHandlerChecksum": "236e47a38077a334e3ae1e7f06314100"}], "pageLayoutTabs": [], "frontComponents": [{"name": "Nodpack for Twenty", "isHeadless": false, "description": "Nodpack for Twenty front component displaying the app logo and name", "componentName": "MainPage", "usesSdkClient": false, "builtComponentPath": "src/front-components/main-page.mjs", "sourceComponentPath": "src/front-components/main-page.tsx", "universalIdentifier": "e9178c9b-b6ea-4cf9-a1df-5411e3717983", "builtComponentChecksum": "5edc87fe03ff44afa6fbb2f881ebe755429d498e8f6a2cbad6f9c4c7cb319fd3"}], "permissionFlags": [], "commandMenuItems": [], "pageLayoutWidgets": [], "settingsMenuItems": [], "connectionProviders": [], "navigationMenuItems": [{"icon": "IconFile", "name": "Nodpack for Twenty", "type": "PAGE_LAYOUT", "position": -1, "universalIdentifier": "4adaf178-f587-4d9f-aec0-d1b881e71fdd", "pageLayoutUniversalIdentifier": "984c2456-1b2f-4f2b-9870-da5ce117cb07"}], "timelineActivityTypes": []}	f	f	public/logo.png	Sets up the objects, fields, views and role the Nodpack mobile app needs in your Twenty workspace.	\N	\N	\N	# Nodpack for Twenty\n\nA companion [Twenty](https://twenty.com) app for [Nodpack](https://nodpack.com), the mobile CRM app for Twenty. It is planned as a **schema-only pack**: it would set up the objects, fields, views and role that Nodpack needs in a Twenty workspace (message templates, logged calls and texts), so every workspace gets the same defaults, with no logic functions so that it can install on a stock self-hosted Twenty as well as on Twenty Cloud. Whether it becomes the setup path is decided in TWE-100.\n\nNodpack is an independent product of Protomated. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Twenty.\n\nStatus (Oct 2026): scaffolded, not yet modelled. The spike that decides whether this pack is the setup path for Nodpack (TWE-99, TWE-100) is in progress. Work is tracked in Nifty, project **TWE**.\n\n## What is here\n\n| Path | What |\n|---|---|\n| `src/` | The app: application config, default role, constants; objects, fields, views and navigation items go here as they are added. |\n| `src/__tests__/` | Unit tests and integration tests (the latter need a Twenty server). |\n| `public/`, `locales/` | App logo (`logo.png`, Protomated's mark) and translations. |\n| `docs/design/research/` | Numbered notes: what the app is for, what it may contain, and what the spike must prove. |\n| `docs/dev/` | Developer guides: [publishing and claiming](docs/dev/publishing.md). |\n| `docs/gtm/` | [Naming rules](docs/gtm/01-naming-rules.md) for the app's public name. |\n| `.github/workflows/` | CI, a deploy-and-install check, and npm publishing with provenance. |\n\nDocumentation index: [docs/README.md](docs/README.md). Coding agents: see [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).\n\n## Getting started\n\nSetup steps are in [SETUP.md](SETUP.md). In short:\n\n```sh\nyarn install\nyarn twenty docker:start   # local Twenty at http://localhost:2020\nyarn twenty dev            # sync the app and watch for changes\n```\n\nCheck your work with `yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck`, `yarn test:unit` and (with the server running) `yarn test`.\n\n## Publishing\n\nThe `Publish` workflow publishes to npm with provenance using [npm trusted publishing](https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers). Publishing from this public repo is also what lets a Twenty admin claim the app. Steps, owners and gotchas: [docs/dev/publishing.md](docs/dev/publishing.md).\n\n## Working on it\n\n- Branches: `twe-<n>/<short-name>` for the Nifty task, merged into `main` with a merge commit.\n- Commit messages: `TWE-<n>: <what changed, in plain words>`, with a body that says why.\n- This repo is public. Do not commit secrets, real customer data or internal planning material.\n\n## Changelog\n\nNotable changes are documented in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).\n\n## Licence\n\nApache-2.0. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n\n## Learn more\n\n- [Twenty Apps documentation](https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/apps/getting-started/quick-start)\n- [twenty-sdk CLI reference](https://www.npmjs.com/package/twenty-sdk)\n- [Twenty Discord](https://discord.gg/cx5n4Jzs57)\n	\N	\N	\N	{}	[{"path": "public/cover.generated.png", "fileId": "e09724cf-b7ef-4f4a-9778-3ef5b28e62bc"}]	3d188e87-74b9-4d08-8588-fdc942425a3a	\N
1312ff82-d8b4-4371-9eb5-9417deae097d	2b7f4a2e-9c4b-4a11-b63c-2e5e7d3f5a9a	Exa	24bcd81b-118e-4c93-bc52-ca44c2bf49f0	\N	{}	{}	\N	2026-10-31 12:36:10.648459+00	2026-10-31 13:26:45.000026+00	\N	\N	npm	@twentyhq/exa	\N	0.2.0	f	{"roles": [{"label": "Exa function role", "description": "No-op role for the exa_web_search logic function", "fieldPermissions": [], "objectPermissions": [], "universalIdentifier": "9a55f3d2-f87c-4f1b-a0f3-5d1c6b8a2e4c", "canBeAssignedToUsers": false, "canUpdateAllSettings": false, "canBeAssignedToAgents": false, "canBeAssignedToApiKeys": false, "canReadAllObjectRecords": false, "canUpdateAllObjectRecords": false, "canDestroyAllObjectRecords": false, "rowLevelPermissionPredicates": [], "canSoftDeleteAllObjectRecords": false, "rowLevelPermissionPredicateGroups": [], "permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers": []}], "views": [], "agents": [], "fields": [], "skills": [], "indexes": [], "objects": [], "viewFields": [], "application": {"logo": "public/exa-logomark.svg", "author": "Twenty", "category": "Search", "termsUrl": "https://www.twenty.com/terms", "websiteUrl": "https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/apps/getting-started", "description": "Structured web search powered by Exa. Surfaces entity-aware results (companies, people, research, news) to Twenty AI agents.", "displayName": "Exa", "emailSupport": "contact@twenty.com", "galleryImages": ["public/cover.generated.png"], "issueReportUrl": "https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues", "serverVariables": {"EXA_API_KEY": {"isSecret": true, "isRequired": true, "description": "Exa API key. Set by the server admin on this registration after installation; the value is injected into every logic function execution."}}, "aboutDescription": "# Exa\\n\\nStructured web search powered by [Exa](https://exa.ai), available to Twenty's AI agents as the `exa_web_search` tool. When an agent needs fresh, entity-aware information from the web (companies, people, research, news, and more), it can call Exa directly from chat and answer with live results.\\n\\n## What it does\\n\\nThis app adds a single AI tool, `exa_web_search`, to your workspace. Twenty AI agents can invoke it to run a search through Exa and receive structured, entity-aware results. It is designed to surface high-quality matches for companies, people, research papers, news, and similar entities rather than generic page links.\\n\\nThe tool reads no workspace data. It only uses the search query the agent provides and your configured Exa API key, calling Exa's external API to return results.\\n\\n## How agents use it\\n\\nThe tool accepts the following inputs:\\n\\n- **query** (required) — the search query to send to Exa.\\n- **category** (optional) — narrows results to a specific type. Supported values: `company`, `research paper`, `news`, `pdf`, `personal site`, `financial report`, `people`. When omitted, Exa searches across all types.\\n- **numResults** (optional) — how many results to return, between `1` and `30`. Defaults to `10`.\\n\\nAgents choose these values automatically based on what they are trying to find, so no manual configuration is needed once the app is set up.\\n\\n## Setup\\n\\nThe app requires an Exa API key, configured once by the server administrator:\\n\\n- **EXA_API_KEY** (required, secret) — your Exa API key. It is set on the app after installation and injected into every search. There is no per-workspace configuration; the same key serves all searches.\\n\\nIf the key is not set, searches fail with an error until an administrator provides it.\\n\\n## Billing\\n\\nEach successful search consumes credits, mirroring Exa's auto-search pricing: a base cost of **$0.007** covers the first 10 results, plus **$0.001** for each additional result. Charges are based on the number of results actually returned, not the number requested.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\n- Returns at most 30 results per search.\\n- Results come live from Exa's external API, so the app depends on Exa's availability and on a valid API key being configured.\\n- The tool only performs web search; it does not read from or write to your workspace data.\\n", "yarnLockChecksum": "ed356fb8250428c8ea25a39544843a99", "packageJsonChecksum": "e869c7c993ffcf9326931854b752d12a", "universalIdentifier": "2b7f4a2e-9c4b-4a11-b63c-2e5e7d3f5a9a", "requiredServerVersionRange": ">=2.19.0", "defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier": "9a55f3d2-f87c-4f1b-a0f3-5d1c6b8a2e4c"}, "pageLayouts": [], "publicAssets": [{"checksum": "b7a8fd3150e12a13c707ba1cdb7598f0", "fileName": "exa-logo.svg", "filePath": "public/exa-logo.svg", "fileType": "svg"}, {"checksum": "29daf8074f6c4ef294a48d4c549b1a2c", "fileName": "exa-logomark.svg", "filePath": "public/exa-logomark.svg", "fileType": "svg"}, {"checksum": "abc5b606572b96e06f44328b0c3fd267", "fileName": "cover.generated.png", "filePath": "public/cover.generated.png", "fileType": "png"}], "logicFunctions": [{"name": "exa_web_search", "description": "Structured web search powered by Exa. Returns entity-aware results with category filtering (companies, people, research papers, news, and other content types). Prefer this when the query benefits from structured data or a specific category. For general real-time web browsing, prefer the native `web_search` tool when it is available.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/exa-web-search.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/exa-web-search.ts", "toolTriggerSettings": {"inputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["query"], "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "The search query to look up on the web. Be specific and include relevant keywords for better results."}, "category": {"enum": ["company", "research paper", "news", "pdf", "personal site", "financial report", "people"], "type": "string", "description": "Optional content category to focus the search. Use \\"company\\" for business/organization info, \\"people\\" for person profiles, \\"news\\" for recent articles, \\"research paper\\" for academic content."}, "numResults": {"type": "integer", "maximum": 30, "minimum": 1, "description": "Number of search results to return. Defaults to 10, max 30. Use more results when you need comprehensive coverage."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}, "universalIdentifier": "4c6f9b2a-5d8e-4c2a-af18-3e0b9c6a7e4f", "builtHandlerChecksum": "6016f478c06dea4a95f61be693266ec6"}], "pageLayoutTabs": [], "frontComponents": [], "permissionFlags": [], "commandMenuItems": [], "connectionProviders": [], "navigationMenuItems": []}	t	f	public/exa-logomark.svg	Structured web search powered by Exa. Surfaces entity-aware results (companies, people, research, news) to Twenty AI agents.	Twenty	Search	https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/apps/getting-started	# Exa\n\nStructured web search powered by [Exa](https://exa.ai), available to Twenty's AI agents as the `exa_web_search` tool. When an agent needs fresh, entity-aware information from the web (companies, people, research, news, and more), it can call Exa directly from chat and answer with live results.\n\n## What it does\n\nThis app adds a single AI tool, `exa_web_search`, to your workspace. Twenty AI agents can invoke it to run a search through Exa and receive structured, entity-aware results. It is designed to surface high-quality matches for companies, people, research papers, news, and similar entities rather than generic page links.\n\nThe tool reads no workspace data. It only uses the search query the agent provides and your configured Exa API key, calling Exa's external API to return results.\n\n## How agents use it\n\nThe tool accepts the following inputs:\n\n- **query** (required) — the search query to send to Exa.\n- **category** (optional) — narrows results to a specific type. Supported values: `company`, `research paper`, `news`, `pdf`, `personal site`, `financial report`, `people`. When omitted, Exa searches across all types.\n- **numResults** (optional) — how many results to return, between `1` and `30`. Defaults to `10`.\n\nAgents choose these values automatically based on what they are trying to find, so no manual configuration is needed once the app is set up.\n\n## Setup\n\nThe app requires an Exa API key, configured once by the server administrator:\n\n- **EXA_API_KEY** (required, secret) — your Exa API key. It is set on the app after installation and injected into every search. There is no per-workspace configuration; the same key serves all searches.\n\nIf the key is not set, searches fail with an error until an administrator provides it.\n\n## Billing\n\nEach successful search consumes credits, mirroring Exa's auto-search pricing: a base cost of **$0.007** covers the first 10 results, plus **$0.001** for each additional result. Charges are based on the number of results actually returned, not the number requested.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Returns at most 30 results per search.\n- Results come live from Exa's external API, so the app depends on Exa's availability and on a valid API key being configured.\n- The tool only performs web search; it does not read from or write to your workspace data.\n	https://www.twenty.com/terms	contact@twenty.com	https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues	{}	[{"path": "public/cover.generated.png", "fileId": "9c9660dd-118f-4020-8524-d6b208240901"}]	e90018af-b939-4476-967f-4d5bee3ff302	\N
