-eec6-4dc6-afa8-3549c9602bb6", "builtHandlerChecksum": "2504004324f1472ba32428f3369ad3d5", "httpRouteTriggerSettings": {"path": "/slack-user-links/search", "httpMethod": "POST", "isAuthRequired": true}}, {"name": "slack-assistant-feedback", "description": "Runs in the resolved workspace: stores the thumbs up / thumbs down rating a user left with the feedback buttons under an assistant answer on the matching Slack Assistant Request record.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 15, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-assistant-feedback.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-assistant-feedback.ts", "universalIdentifier": "60947582-0735-4b6d-8c1f-5e237875a2e4", "builtHandlerChecksum": "9382975e920e2f4d4382349f7e88a84f"}, {"name": "slack-health-check", "description": "Reports a broken Slack connection as a banner on the app settings page, whichever tab is open: the stored token no longer passes auth.test, or the installed Slack team is claimed by another Twenty workspace, so its messages are delivered elsewhere.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/health-check.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/health-check.ts", "universalIdentifier": "7c303a5c-80ff-4e27-9997-c6c14239c0ba", "builtHandlerChecksum": "15e5a9f89fbd12e4cc99b44a4d1cd2b6"}, {"name": "slack-list-unlinked-users", "description": "Lists Slack workspace users that have no Slack user link yet so an admin can link them manually. Restricted to members with the roles permission.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 60, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-list-unlinked-users.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-list-unlinked-users.ts", "universalIdentifier": "7cd303b1-da18-4f68-895a-b01bca2f0381", "builtHandlerChecksum": "916b11ead548d72a854a510e2157c1c3", "httpRouteTriggerSettings": {"path": "/slack-user-links/unlinked", "httpMethod": "POST", "isAuthRequired": true}}, {"name": "slack-assistant-request", "description": "Runs in the resolved workspace: records the Slack message as a Slack Assistant Request, then answers it in the same execution by showing a native thinking status on the conversation thread, running the Slack Assistant agent against the workspace, and posting the answer as a threaded reply.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 240, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-assistant-request.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-assistant-request.ts", "universalIdentifier": "8f2e1d3c-4b5a-4c6d-9e7f-0a1b2c3d4e5f", "builtHandlerChecksum": "ff1f789ccbfa49eafa3382b8d2aa16b0"}, {"name": "slack-resolve-user-link", "description": "Resolves a Slack account from an email or Slack user id so an admin can confirm the right person before linking. Restricted to members with the roles permission.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-resolve-user-link.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-resolve-user-link.ts", "universalIdentifier": "92e1291a-c416-4294-b2f7-2db992322988", "builtHandlerChecksum": "ff04bdccb5398ee7d81ed170dfb94094", "httpRouteTriggerSettings": {"path": "/slack-user-links/resolve", "httpMethod": "POST", "isAuthRequired": true}}, {"name": "slack-events-resolver", "description": "Receives Slack Events API callbacks, verifies the request signature in the owner workspace, answers the url_verification handshake, and resolves the target workspace plus the function that handles the event (assistant enqueue, the channel welcome on member_joined_channel, the suggested prompts on app_home_opened, the record link previews on link_shared and entity_details_requested, or the team release on app_uninstalled and tokens_revoked).", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 15, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-events-resolver.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-events-resolver.ts", "universalIdentifier": "9ad6fa20-dff5-4d3f-ad5f-084f3c8b0b09", "builtHandlerChecksum": "e9810be0d273a596a6ed11608e33cdf6", "serverRouteTriggerSettings": {"forwardedRequestHeaders": ["x-slack-signature", "x-slack-request-timestamp", "x-slack-retry-num", "x-slack-retry-reason"]}}, {"name": "slack-register-connection", "description": "Runs when a Slack connection is established (via the connection provider onConnect hook). Resolves the Slack team_id for the just-created connection via auth.test and stores this workspace id under the server-scoped slack-team:<team_id> key so inbound Slack events route here. Records the same team under slack-connected-account-team:<connected_account_id> so the disconnect hook can release the claim once the connection is gone. Caches the bot user id from the same auth.test under slack-bot-user-id so the channel welcome can recognise the bot without calling Slack on every join event. Links the installer and then sweeps the Slack roster for members whose confirmed email matches a workspace member, which is why this hook needs the same budget as the on-demand match route.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 120, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-register-connection.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-register-connection.ts", "universalIdentifier": "a29ae15d-dd16-4b99-bb6c-079842da55ab", "builtHandlerChecksum": "d7634c1cbd1f2b038e9778a0467a0e73"}, {"name": "slack-link-unfurl", "description": "Runs in the resolved workspace: renders Twenty record links shared in Slack as work object previews, when the poster maps to a workspace member.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 15, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-link-unfurl.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-link-unfurl.ts", "universalIdentifier": "b9126247-b6f3-4c1f-a4c5-1c7b28d4beea", "builtHandlerChecksum": "8184aca47e2be0d82479496c4e84dd18"}, {"name": "slack-channel-welcome", "description": "Runs in the resolved workspace: posts a one-off introduction when the bot itself is added to a Slack channel.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 15, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-channel-welcome.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-channel-welcome.ts", "universalIdentifier": "c5e8b13a-7f42-4d90-8a6b-1e3c9d052f47", "builtHandlerChecksum": "a4e04fb5f2cfa8d8f1142d60f1ddeb90"}, {"name": "slack-post-message", "description": "Send a message to a Slack channel or DM. Optionally reply inside an existing thread using the parent message’s timestamp from a previous step.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-post-message.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-post-message.ts", "toolTriggerSettings": {"inputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["slackChannelId", "messageText"], "properties": {"messageText": {"type": "string", "label": "Message", "multiline": true, "description": "The message people will read in Slack. Keep it concise; very long messages may be rejected by Slack."}, "messageFormat": {"enum": ["plain", "markdown"], "type": "string", "label": "Message format", "description": "Optional. `markdown`: send as Slack `markdown_text` so usual Markdown in `messageText` works (**bold**, lists, fenced code). `plain`: send as `text` with `mrkdwn: false` (no markup). Omit: send as `text` and let Slack use its default (legacy mrkdwn may still apply in `text`)."}, "slackChannelId": {"type": "string", "label": "Slack channel (name or ID)", "description": "Where to post: the Slack channel or DM ID (looks like C0123…, G… for private channels, or D… for DMs). In Slack: open the channel → channel name → scroll down → copy Channel ID. Using the ID is more reliable than a channel name."}, "parentMessageTimestamp": {"type": "string", "label": "Parent message timestamp", "description": "Optional. Only when you want a **thread reply**: paste the **Message timestamp** from an earlier Slack step (the value returned as `slackTs` after posting). Leave empty for a normal new message at the bottom of the channel."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}, "universalIdentifier": "c6f25d09-1b7c-4e3f-ad42-7aec5b29830f", "builtHandlerChecksum": "95d1babe5d6d9c9beca7da7cfe20e7e0", "workflowActionTriggerSettings": {"icon": "IconBrandSlack", "label": "Send Slack Message", "inputSchema": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"messageText": {"type": "string", "label": "Message", "multiline": true}, "messageFormat": {"enum": ["plain", "markdown"], "type": "string", "label": "Message format"}, "slackChannelId": {"type": "string", "label": "Slack channel (name or ID)"}, "parentMessageTimestamp": {"type": "string", "label": "Parent message timestamp"}}}], "outputSchema": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"error": {"type": "string"}, "channel": {"type": "string"}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "slackTs": {"type": "string"}, "success": {"type": "boolean"}}}]}}, {"name": "slack-connection-status", "description": "Tells the settings tab whether a Slack workspace connection exists and whether it is healthy: the stored token still passes auth.test, and the installed Slack team is claimed by this Twenty workspace so events route here. The tab hides the link management tools until Slack is connected and while the connection is broken, which the app health check reports as a banner on the settings page.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-connection-status.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-connection-status.ts", "universalIdentifier": "ca8af663-5229-486a-b81b-1ac9bf8e1e8f", "builtHandlerChecksum": "fea73e49c9a32fc462e744eea494e1dc", "httpRouteTriggerSettings": {"path": "/slack-user-links/connection-status", "httpMethod": "POST", "isAuthRequired": true}}, {"name": "slack-deliver-message", "description": "Posts a single Slack message that was rate limited on its first attempt. Enqueued with the delay Slack asked for, so the calling function never waits on a 429.", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-deliver-message.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-deliver-message.ts", "universalIdentifier": "cc43a728-7b9f-43c6-a9a2-bd1196204822", "builtHandlerChecksum": "01c57daac2e4a778d686a67a47b66e12"}, {"name": "slack-post-ephemeral-message", "description": "Send a private-on-channel note: only the chosen teammate sees it in that channel (not a DM broadcast to everyone).", "handlerName": "default.config.handler", "timeoutSeconds": 30, "builtHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-post-ephemeral-message.mjs", "sourceHandlerPath": "src/logic-functions/slack-post-ephemeral-message.ts", "toolTriggerSettings": {"inputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["slackChannelId", "recipientSlackUserId", "messageText"], "properties": {"messageText": {"type": "string", "label": "Message", "multiline": true, "description": "Short note shown only to the recipient above — for example a private hint, validation result, or next step."}, "messageFormat": {"enum": ["plain", "markdown"], "type": "string", "label": "Message format", "description": "Optional. Same as **Send Slack Message**: `markdown` / `plain` / omit — see that action’s `messageFormat` description."}, "slackChannelId": {"type": "string", "label": "Slack channel (name or ID)", "description": "Channel where the note appears (Slack channel ID like C…). The person you choose must already be in this channel, or they will not see the message."}, "recipientSlackUserId": {"type": "string", "label": "Recipient (Slack user ID)", "description": "Who can see this message: their Slack **member ID** (starts with U…). Only that person sees it; everyone else in the channel does not. In Slack: click their profile → three 